WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.890
<i>The cultural festival is almost here!</i>

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.080
<i>Our earth sciences club is working 
hard to get ready for it.</i>

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.480
<i>Our geology members, 
Sakura-senpai and Ino-senpai,</i>

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.950
<i>will be attempting a major experiment.</i>

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:16.620
All right!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.080
Oh, it's started, eh?

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.540
What has?

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.860
An extension of the agar experiment.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.220
06. Hoshizaki Festival!

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.220
Inose, what's that?

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.600
Eve-chan. Usami-san, too.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:11.200
We're collecting info for a 
special cultural festival issue.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.610
And... what's that?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.190
It's the earth sciences club's 
original boring machine!

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.030
Oh, nice! It really stands out!

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.530
But it looks too shabby to call a machine.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:28.170
Wow, it combines a simple design 
with affordability! Fantastic!

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.670
This is for that survey you 
were talking about before?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.830
Yeah. It's just a simple one, though.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.840
A simple one?

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.670
Yes.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.300
Ow!

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.570
In a formal survey,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.600
an actual standard penetration test, 
there are all kinds of regulations.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.730
Like the weight of the hammer, 
N-value measurements, and so on.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.900
But instead of worrying about that,

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.150
we narrowed our goal down to 
just boring out a core sample.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.230
I see. Makes no sense to me!

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.840
Don't act so confident 
if you don't understand!

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.260
Anyway, where are the astronomy girls today?

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.090
It looks like you could use their help.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.910
They'd just get in the way.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.580
We're more than enough.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.440
What she means is that she 
doesn't want to bother them

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.380
while they're busy with other preparations.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.630
Hmm...

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.280
Cute, isn't she?

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.570
Huh...

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.050
Okay, then!

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.430
Back to work we go. Clear out.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.480
It's finally a quarter of the way in?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.880
Want to switch, Senpai?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.940
No, I'm fine.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.320
Hey, you two!

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.520
The newspaper club brought help!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.700
What should we be doing, Sakurai-san?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.720
Huh? Wh-What?

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.750
U-Um...

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.790
Senpai, since they're here, 
why don't we let them help?

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.250
Uh, i-in that case...

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.680
Are you all confident in your strength?

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:55.960
Here we go!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.670
One, two!

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.590
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.590
Wow, it's so light.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:03.490
Heave-ho!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.970
Heave-ho!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.950
So this is what your club does, Sakurai-san?

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.360
Heave-ho!

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:10.750
Heave-ho!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.130
I don't really get it, but it seems fun.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.310
Heave-ho!

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.940
I had no idea at all.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.820
Heave-ho!

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.900
You're always such a mysterious, 
cool character in our class.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.660
Can you tell me more about that?

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.660
Heave-ho!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.360
Ino, focus!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.320
Heave-ho!

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.750
Heave-ho!

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.280
Heave-ho!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.720
Heave-ho!

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.950
Just a little more!

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.120
Heave-ho!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.620
Heave-ho!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.140
Heave-ho!

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.570
Heave-ho!

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.340
<i>"I don't really get it, but it seems fun," huh?</i>

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:42.990
Heave-ho!

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.900
<i>I always just assumed my classmates</i>

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:51.220
<i>wouldn't understand my 
interests or the club, but...</i>

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:52.880
Heave-ho!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.230
It's practically impossible 
for a tiny club like ours.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.710
We can't do that. It's not realistic.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.240
<i>But it really is a waste to 
just decide it's impossible</i>

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.520
Heave-ho!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.240
Heave-ho!

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.610
<i>before I even try.</i>

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.610
Heave-ho!

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.700
We've reached our goal!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:15.870
We did it!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.250
So how do we pull this pipe back out?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.150
Oh, uh...

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.160
Sakurai-san.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:24.550
Can we use these?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.950
They're the fittings used in the 
baseball club's practice nets.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.010
Let me see those.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:32.970
One, two!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.540
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.980
Thank you all so much!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.650
Sure!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:42.920
Good luck!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.230
Well, we'll be getting back to practice.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.230
Later!

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.450
Having them come by was a huge help.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.210
I bet you're surprised by the 
breadth of our connections!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.180
Yeah.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.460
Like you said, we needed more people.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.460
Thank you so much.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:01.920
Hey!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.230
Working hard?

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.180
Sensei!

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.200
Thank you for giving us permission.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.790
Thank you!

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:08.930
It's fine.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.870
None of that formal stuff.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.430
So, did you get your core?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.330
Yes. It's inside the pipe.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.760
We need to push it out with that pole.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.230
What's important here is momentum.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.940
One, two!

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.150
S-Sensei...

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.360
It was supposed to be a cylinder!

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.920
S-S-S-Sorry! I'm sorry!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.420
Sensei, that was terrible! Just terrible!

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.420
S-Senpai?

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:46.840
It's done!

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.340
Ta-da! It's Earth!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.870
That's really good, Mira.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.100
We're going to have a nice solar system.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.030
Thank you!

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:01.720
Ao, are you having trouble? Should I help?

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:02.610
Nah.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.520
I'm fine.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.710
I love Jupiter, so I want 
to finish it up myself.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.260
Uh, just a piece of advice, then?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.760
Remember to breathe.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:18.000
Jupiter is lovely, isn't it? The patterns, 
the size of its moons... everything!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.150
Yeah. I was so impressed when I saw 
it through my telescope as a child.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.790
Unlike when I saw it in pictures,

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.310
I really felt that it was actually there.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.630
I can relate.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:34.120
It's so much fun to notice the moons are 
moving when you observe them over time.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:34.960
Yeah!

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.720
Saturn's done!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.960
I finished one, too.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.110
The moon!

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.080
It took some time, though.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.090
There are mountains, seas, and craters on it.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.190
Monroe-senpai, this is really detailed!

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:52.500
<i>But at this pace, we won't 
reach our quota for today.</i>

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.410
On to the next ones!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.680
Uranus and Neptune don't have 
much of a pattern on them.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:05.140
What's your favorite planet in 
the solar system, Monroe-senpai?

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.960
Hmm... My number one would be the moon.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.920
<i>So it's more detailed because she likes it more.</i>

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.730
It's so bright and pretty, isn't it?

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:14.550
Yes, and also...

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.840
"It's the furthest point 
humans have stood on."

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:20.560
"But it's the closest planet to Earth."

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.690
That's what my grandma always used to say.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:27.360
I got my love of astronomy from her.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.790
Your grandmother loved astronomy, too?

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.320
Yeah. When I was just a little girl...

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.120
People's passion for space 
exploration at the time

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.550
had everyone glued to their 
televisions watching.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.790
I'd love to try hopping 
around the moon like that.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.750
I'm sure everyone will be 
able to visit space one day!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:51.480
By the time that happens, 
I'll be old and weak.

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:55.240
Though, to tell you the truth, 
I've bought some land.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:55.970
Land?

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.960
Some land on the moon.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.550
It's where I'll have my grave.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:05.190
Did you decide to become an 
astronaut after hearing that?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.060
Yeah. It was one of the reasons, I think.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.910
This is my grandma.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.190
Your dream is a dream that's been 
handed down through generations.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.780
Yeah, I suppose so.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:21.830
We talked about having a video chat over 
our smartphones if I make it to space.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.370
Wow, even your grandma 
is surpassing generations.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.540
Oh, it's already dark out.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.370
Wow, it's in the perfect spot for viewing!

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.800
It's almost time for the harvest moon.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:36.760
Here.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.340
Thank you!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.980
Wow, incredible!

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.800
It's so pretty!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.680
Um, um... The time!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.020
We need to work!

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:46.850
It's done!

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.610
Here's our last one, Venus!

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.920
You're really fast, Mira!

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.070
Now most of the models are complete.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.840
That just leaves preparing the display board.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:00.440
Since we're running a café, we'll 
want to make the interior cute, too.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:03.440
If we put earth science 
magazines on each table,

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:05.540
it'll give people something 
fun to do while they wait.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.230
Let's see, what else?

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.700
You have so many fun ideas!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.960
Our dreams are expanding!

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:17.800
<i>Her head's in the clouds, 
just like an astronaut.</i>

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.590
Well, that's enough work for today.

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:24.250
We'll talk to the geology 
girls about the next steps.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.780
Roger that!

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:26.310
<i>Huh?</i>

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.310
<i>I thought we were behind on our work,</i>

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.310
<i>but we're exactly at the time we set.</i>

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.960
<i>Has Senpai been keeping 
time without us knowing?</i>

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:35.440
Hmm?

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.070
Oh, it's nothing.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:38.900
<i>No way.</i>

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:40.950
So pretty.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.530
Shall we turn the lights 
off for a better view?

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.580
It's strange how I just never grow 
tired of looking at the starry sky.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:53.280
Yeah. I get so caught up in it, I forget to sleep.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.540
There's a really nice smell, too...

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:05.160
Even if you forget to sleep, 
you won't forget to eat.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.780
Suzu-chan, what are you doing?!

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.730
You were all so busy looking outside 
that you didn't even notice me.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.540
I brought the test samples for the café.

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.340
It's a shame the geology girls aren't here,

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:24.200
but if you could rate the taste, shape, color, 
texture, and smell on a scale of one to ten—

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.890
Let's eat!

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.450
Thanks for the treat!

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.960
I'll have another tasting before the day, 
so it's fine for now, but...

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.920
S-Sorry. I was just so hungry...

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.920
So, is everything ready?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.670
Yeah. That's why we were gazing at the moon.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.640
Yeah, it's clear tonight, 
so it looks really pretty.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:48.680
It's a first quarter moon.
Lunar age 7.9, was it?

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.970
That's what it said in the 
magazine Ao gave me.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.350
Ao, you're so forward!

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.980
I think she's just touched that you read it.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.690
Ah, what a nice smell!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.600
Moon-viewing and nice smells gave me an idea!

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.800
Mira! Can I add something to the menu?

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:10.750
That's perfectly fine, but, um...

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:12.720
Could you put Ao down?

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:13.550
Oh.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:16.900
Also, Monroe-senpai, please stop 
taking photos of everything.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:17.710
Oh.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:22.270
<i>That's the first time I've missed
 Sakura-senpai's quips.</i>

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.620
<b>Hoshizaki High School 
Cultural Festival</b>

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.560
<b>Hoshizaki High School 
Cultural Festival</b>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:35.020
<b>Hoshizaki Festival</b>

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.230
<i>These themes don't go together at all.</i>

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.600
It's a pretty café now!

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.740
My, my, my!

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.250
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.850
<i>I'm not sure how well it works as a café,</i>

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:56.030
I hope we'll get lots of customers.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.170
<i>but this mixed-up feel is 
the club's selling point.</i>

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.640
<i>Well, I guess it'll all work out.</i>

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>The Hoshizaki High School 
Cultural Festival will now begin.</i>

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.010
All right, everyone!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.440
Let's do our best!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.310
Suzu-san, we appreciate your help today.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:15.210
I can't believe you're helping us 
on the day of the festival, too.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.020
It's nothing!

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.860
You seem more into this than we are.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.260
The truth is, there's also this project.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.780
<b>Best Taste Contest</b>

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.780
<b>Will you be this year's best-tasting stall?!</b>

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.780
A food stall contest!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:29.080
If we win this, it'll be the perfect 
advertisement for our shop, too!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.790
Suzu-chan, you're making 
a really bad impression.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.300
Oh, welcome!

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.420
Wait, it's you, Sensei?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.960
Sorry I'm not your first customer.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.920
I didn't do a final check on your 
displays earlier, so I need to be quick.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:55.230
No problem with the length 
of your skirts, either.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:58.190
Well, if I decide to check again,
 I'll come back.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.360
She ate everything on the menu and left.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.920
She'll be back at snack time.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:08.490
<b>Pegmatite Scone
Milky Way Gelatin
Boring Tiramisu
Planet Cookies
Waxing Moon Pancakes</b>

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:08.490
Please order over here.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.320
What do you recommend?

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:15.000
You can enjoy eight different flavors 
with these planet cookies.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:18.710
I also recommend the Milky Way 
gelatin, since it's photogenic.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:23.270
Pardon me! Try some of our 
geology group's sweets, too!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.670
This tiramisu lets you try boring for yourself.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.630
Enjoy it by sucking it through the straw.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.660
That sounds fun. I'll try that.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.640
Me, too! We'll take two of the tiramisu!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.770
Two boring tiramisu, then. 
Thank you very much!

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:43.940
Um, could we have a spoon?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.090
Huh?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:47.860
Hello.

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:51.200
Oh. Welcome, reporters.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.070
We'll be taking a few notes!

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.060
Wow, they all look so good!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.500
<b>Pegmatite Scone</b>

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.500
<b>We made them based on pegmatite!
Pegmatite is a pretty, sparkly stone. To capture that sparkle,
 we used chocolate chips and berries,
and then baked them into a scone to simulate the rocky look!

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.500
Pegmatite Scone?

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:00.370
It's the name of a rock.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.680
When magma slowly cools and hardens,

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:05.780
it can become a stone with large crystals in it.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.370
That's pegmatite.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.470
It's more commonly known 
as the "Image of a Demon."

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.620
That shares part of Vice 
President Sakurai's name.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:16.970
Then that makes this sweet the 
Demon Vice President's Scone!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.490
That's a good one! You get a floor cushion!

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:29.150
There are roughly 8,600 stars that can 
be seen from Earth with the naked eye,

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.680
but there are more than 200 
billion in the Milky Way.

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.120
Wow, over 200 billion...

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:35.120
Huh? That many? That's incredible.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.840
Monroe-senpai, it's amazing how 
detailed your explanations are!

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:39.980
Thanks.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:44.260
I actually wrote down the numbers and 
terms I was likely to forget in a memo.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:45.380
Wow.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.740
I made some memos, too, 
since I tend to get nervous.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.090
Oh!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.880
Excuse me, I have a question.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.970
Y-Yes?

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.800
N-Nice to meet you.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:59.430
I'm Manaka Ao from the earth 
sciences club's astronomy group.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.390
I hope you're all enjoying the 
fun world of astronomy today.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.390
It's a script?

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:05.280
This is our handmade model.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:08.360
The sizes and distances 
involved in the solar system

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.360
would make it bigger than the classroom, 
so it's a bit distorted.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.120
Are those lines shooting stars?

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:17.770
One is the habitable zone, 
and the other is the asteroid belt.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:20.650
Then is that fluffy thing a cloud?

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.580
It's the Edgeworth-Kuiper Belt.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.600
Whee! You're on a journey through space!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.140
Wow! Yay!

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.200
Go, go, go!

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.780
So fast!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.680
Sakura-senpai, are you looking for someone?

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:43.400
Well...

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:48.210
My classmates who helped with the boring 
said they'd stop by to check us out.

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:49.650
Really?!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:53.330
Then I'll manage the shop while 
you go handle explanations!

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.200
Yoo-hoo.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.910
I'm here, Sakurai-san.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.620
Welcome.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.190
Senpai—huh?

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.630
W-Welcome.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:03.870
Sakura-senpai?

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:04.780
Hey!

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:08.480
Wow, I always thought the earth 
sciences club was, like, stiffer.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.840
Oh, this is the core sample 
we extracted that day.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.720
Embankment

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.720
Clay

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.720
Silt

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:14.720
So this is how it turned out?

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:18.060
Beneath the embankment, 
there's a layer of mud and clay,

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:20.970
so we can hypothesize that this 
area used to be a rice paddy.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:24.480
Oh! Is that why the drainage is 
so bad on the school grounds?

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:25.940
Possibly.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.990
Huh? I heard this area was a graveyard 
before the school was built.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.900
I've heard that, too.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:33.360
Ino?!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:37.160
There were rumors that the drainage 
is bad because the ghost of a woman

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.320
who was cruelly rejected keeps crying here.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.330
I've heard that one, too!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.540
Ino?! What does that say 
about our geology group?!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.500
Hey.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.500
W-Welcome!

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:51.220
Onee-chan, you're the head judge today?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.720
Yeah, I heard the earth sciences 
club's pancakes are popular.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:55.880
I'd like to try one.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:00.460
Suzu-chan, are you okay? Are you nervous?

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:04.230
I can't believe I get to feed 
Misa-nee freshly baked food!

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.270
I'll give it my best effort!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.280
We'll get disqualified for bribery!

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.200
Here are your Waxing Moon Pancakes.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.530
We've reproduced today's moon phase
with our specially made fresh cream.

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:20.960
Time to try some.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:25.680
By the way, the flavor is honey milk, 
the same as the scent of Ao's hair!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.770
Suzu-san, you don't need to say that!

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:33.450
A fluffy texture, the scent of Ao-kun's hair,

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:37.840
and this really sweet, delicious flavor...

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.440
Thank you for the meal.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.480
It was very well-made.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.520
Was that a tasting report?

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:50.270
Misa-nee doesn't know how to handle 
things that can't be put into numbers.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:53.230
The earth sciences club's display looks nice.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.210
It was definitely worth helping out.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.210
Onee-chan...

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.780
All we did was pull up some rocks, though!

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:00.150
You're not supposed to say that.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:05.580
Oh, speaking of which, the pancakes 
at the manga club were amazing!

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:05.010
Onee-chan...

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:05.580
Huh?

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.500
Yeah, but there was a huge line, 
so I gave up on trying to get in.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.210
Chikage?

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.550
Was I just imagining it?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.830
Onee-chan's wonderful at school, too.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:24.390
Oh? So this is our solar system?

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.790
It's all hand-made? That's incredible.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:31.340
Thanks! We had a lot of fun making these!

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:34.340
This isn't nearly enough.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.040
Thank you for visiting!

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.010
Mira!

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:45.370
Mom?! Dad?!

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:49.080
Misa told us your pancakes are delicious.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.330
Two orders, please!

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.280
Onee!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.910
Megu, you came!

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:56.780
Yeah.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:59.650
Wow, this is cool. Anything I can help with?

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:01.550
Don't worry, just eat!

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:04.120
Oh, are you Ao-san's mother?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.390
Thank you for taking good 
care of my daughter.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.560
Oh, no, you've taken good care of mine, too.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.840
Mira-san, that outfit looks good on you.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.890
Oh, no! Ao-san is much cuter!

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:17.040
I'm dressed like this in front of my parents...

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.220
Sakura-senpai, do you have any spare tracksuits?

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:21.740
Nope!

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:25.200
Ao, your display turned out great.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.780
Thanks.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.510
So this is what you've been 
doing in your club, huh?

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:32.240
You hardly ever talk about yourself, you know.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.680
That's all the more reason 
I'm glad I came today.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:41.170
Mind if I take a picture of you in 
that outfit to show your father?

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:44.160
No!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.450
<i>I've never heard Ao make that noise before.</i>

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.760
<i>Thank you very much for coming today.</i>

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:56.460
<i>This concludes the Hoshizaki 
High School Cultural Festival.</i>

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.460
I-It's over.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.190
I'm worn out from talking to so many people.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:03.240
This has been the funnest cultural 
festival ever, thanks to all of you.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.860
Right, Sakura-chan?

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.270
Yeah.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.450
Good work, everyone.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.740
Sakura-senpai's being up-front.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.410
It's an omen of natural disaster.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:15.170
You two should accept it up-front, too.

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:16.590
I'm expressing gratitude.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.400
Oh, right.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:21.180
President, you had something 
important to discuss, right?

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.840
That's right. Everyone, listen up.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.930
What is it?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.800
As of today, we're both...

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:31.760
...stepping down as president 
and vice president.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:33.860
Huh?

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:39.230
S-Stepping down?! You're quitting 
the earth sciences club?!

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.700
No, we're stepping down from our roles.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:45.250
We'll still be part of the 
club until we graduate.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:50.400
So, with that, I'd like to ask you 
to be the next president, Ino-chan.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.180
We're counting on you, Ino!

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:58.290
Huh?

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:01.950
What?!

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:39.850
6.5
Recap: <i>Sparkle</i>'s Special Issue

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:39.260
Next time, "Recap: <i>Sparkle</i>'s Special Issue."
